1) MySQL — Sysbench

Pré-requisitos

sudo apt install sysbench mysql-client mysql-server -y


Criar DB

mysql -u root -p -e "CREATE DATABASE energiaTest;"


Preparar 2M operações

sysbench \
  --db-driver=mysql \
  --mysql-user=root \
  --mysql-password=YOURPASS \
  --mysql-db=energiaTest \
  --threads=4 \
  --tables=1 \
  --table-size=2000000 \
  oltp_read_write prepare


Executar 5 blocos (2M cada)

for i in {1..5}; do
  echo "Rodada $i" >> mysql_results.txt
  sysbench \
    --db-driver=mysql \
    --mysql-user=root \
    --mysql-password=YOURPASS \
    --mysql-db=energiaTest \
    --threads=4 \
    --tables=1 \
    --table-size=2000000 \
    --time=0 \
    --events=2000000 \
    oltp_read_write run >> mysql_results.txt
done


Limpeza

sysbench --db-driver=mysql --mysql-user=root --mysql-password=YOURPASS --mysql-db=energiaTest oltp_read_write cleanup

🪶 2) SQLite Script — 10 milhões ops

Instale Python libs

pip install sqlite3 tqdm


sqlite_test.py

import sqlite3, time, random
from tqdm import tqdm

conn = sqlite3.connect("energia_sqlite.db")
c = conn.cursor()
c.execute("CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS teste (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, valor INTEGER);")
conn.commit()

total_ops = 10_000_000
batch = 1000

start = time.time()

for _ in tqdm(range(total_ops//batch)):
    data = [(random.randint(1,999999),) for _ in range(batch)]
    c.executemany("INSERT INTO teste(valor) VALUES (?)", data)
    conn.commit()
    c.execute("SELECT * FROM teste ORDER BY RANDOM() LIMIT 5")
    c.fetchall()

end = time.time()
print("Total time:", end-start, "sec")


Run:

python3 sqlite_test.py | tee sqlite_results.txt

